<!--
  ONE PACKAGE THAT WOLVERINE 6 NEEDS AND CODEGEN DOES NOT EMIT.

  Wolverine 6 removed the runtime compiler from core WolverineFx: with TypeLoadMode.Dynamic and no
  IAssemblyGenerator registered, the host throws at startup (GH-2876). Wolverine 5 shipped it, so
  codegen.mjs has no reason to emit this reference and the kit's other reference implementations do not
  need it.

  package-versions.json overrides the VERSION of a package codegen emits; it cannot ADD one. That is a
  gap worth closing in codegen.mjs — see KIT-FINDINGS AD11.

  Directory.Build.props is imported BEFORE the project body, so a plain PackageReference here is an
  ordinary evaluated item and restore sees it. Note the contrast with the failed attempt recorded in
  AD10: `<PackageReference Update=...>` inside a TARGET is ignored by restore. Adding here is reliable;
  re-versioning there was not.
-->
<Project>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="WolverineFx.RuntimeCompilation" Version="6.*" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
